+
+class DSAPreconditioner:
+    """Approximate ``(I - G)^{-1}`` from the thick-limit moment system.
+
+    ``apply(r) = r + A^{-1} (M r)`` with ``A`` the discretised low-order
+    operator and ``M`` the DG mass matrix.  The ``+r`` is what makes the
+    preconditioner degrade gracefully to the identity in the ballistic limit,
+    where the thick-limit expansion the operator comes from does not hold:
+    there ``A`` grows like ``(k Vg tau_C)^2`` and its inverse vanishes, and a
+    preconditioner that tends to zero would leave GMRES with nothing to work
+    on.
+
+    ``A`` is built in one of two shapes.
+
+    ``decoupled``  ``tau_N >> tau_R``.  N-scattering is too rare to move
+                   energy, the ``T``-``q`` coupling terms carry the factor
+                   ``beta = tau_C/tau_N`` and vanish with it, and the two
+                   blocks are solved separately -- a 1/3-size factorisation.
+    ``coupled``    the hydrodynamic corner, ``tau_R >> tau_N``.  The block
+                   that converges slowly there is *transverse momentum*, and
+                   the energy block only sees it through ``div q``, so the
+                   three fields have to be factorised together.
+    """
